# Compact form layout (design rule)

Calculator input panels must use the **compact form** pattern — not stacked
label-above-input grids — unless an existing tool already uses a specialised
layout (e.g. psychrometric state paste / chart) and is only being patched.

## Required pattern

```html
<form method="get" class="compact-form">
  <fieldset class="compact-group">
    <legend>Group name</legend>
    <div class="compact-row"><!-- or cols-2 / cols-4 -->
      <div class="compact-field">
        <label for="id">Short label</label>
        <input id="id" name="..." ...>
      </div>
      <!-- more short fields on the same row -->
    </div>
  </fieldset>
  <div class="compact-actions">
    <button class="btn-accent" type="submit">…</button>
  </div>
</form>
```

CSS lives in `web/app/static/css/app.css` (`.compact-form`); V2 keeps multi-column
rows via overrides in `v2.css` (do **not** wrap these fields in `.form-grid` —
V2 collapses `.form-grid` to one column).

## Rules

1. **Label + control on one line** — `.compact-field` (fixed-width right-aligned label + input/select).
2. **Align columns** — same label column width across a row; prefer short labels (`Tevap °C`, `SH K`) with `title=` for longer hints.
3. **Group related inputs** — `<fieldset class="compact-group">` + `<legend>` (Duty, Cycle, Pressures, …).
4. **Pack short scalars** — 2–3 (or 4) fields per `.compact-row` when they are single-value entries.
5. **Mobile** — rows collapse to one field per line below ~720px; label stays beside the control.
6. **New modules** — ship compact forms by default. When refactoring older tools, migrate inputs to `.compact-form` rather than adding more `.form-grid` stacks.

## Anti-patterns

- Label on its own line with the input below for every field.
- Empty grid cells used only for spacing.
- Long paragraph labels in the label column — shorten the label; put detail in help text or `title`.
